title: Database Schema Reference
description: Complete column-by-column database schema reference for all 12 LibSQL / Turso tables in Lament.
section: Development
order: 4
---

## Engine & Connection

Lament uses **LibSQL** (SQLite edge engine) hosted on **Turso** (`@libsql/client`). All tables and relationships are defined in `schema.sql`.

---

## Complete Table Specifications

### 1. `artists` (Artist Metadata)

Stores catalog artist profiles and scraper image origin tags.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | TEXT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique artist UUID (e.g. `art_3d8e1f`) |
| `name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Artist display name |
| `slug` | TEXT | UNIQUE, NOT NULL | URL-safe slug (e.g. `tulus`) |
| `image_url` | TEXT | NULL | Processed CDN image URL |
| `image_source` | TEXT | NULL | Provider source tag (`lastfm`, `deezer`, `spotify`) |
| `created_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Record creation timestamp |
| `updated_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Last modification timestamp |

---

### 2. `albums` (Album Collections)

Stores album metadata linked to artists.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | TEXT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique album UUID |
| `artist_id` | TEXT | FOREIGN KEY (artists.id) | Primary artist ID |
| `title` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Album title |
| `slug` | TEXT | NOT NULL | URL-safe slug |
| `cover_url` | TEXT | NULL | Album cover artwork CDN URL |
| `cover_source` | TEXT | NULL | Cover image source provider |
| `year` | INTEGER | NULL | Release year |
| `type` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Collection type (`album`, `ep`, `single`) |
| `description` | TEXT | NULL | Album description notes |
| `created_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Record creation timestamp |
| `updated_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Last modification timestamp |

---

### 3. `categories` (Genres & Tags)

Stores music categories and genre classifications.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | TEXT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique category UUID |
| `name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Category display name (e.g. `Indie Pop`) |
| `slug` | TEXT | UNIQUE, NOT NULL | URL-safe slug |
| `created_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Record creation timestamp |

---

### 4. `tracks` (Core Audio Catalog)

Core table for music tracks, audio formats, bitrates, and anti-duplication IDs.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | TEXT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique track UUID |
| `artist_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL, FK (artists.id) | Primary artist ID |
| `album_id` | TEXT | NULL, FK (albums.id) | Parent album ID |
| `title` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Track title |
| `slug` | TEXT | NOT NULL | URL-safe slug |
| `original_id` | TEXT | UNIQUE | Anti-duplication ID (`yt_<id>` or Spotify ID) |
| `provider_url` | TEXT | NULL | Original source URL |
| `audio_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL | HLS playlist pointer (`hls:<track_id>`) |
| `cover_url` | TEXT | NULL | Track cover artwork URL |
| `cover_source` | TEXT | NULL | Artwork provider source |
| `duration` | INTEGER | NULL | Duration in seconds |
| `bitrate` | INTEGER | NULL | Source audio bitrate (e.g. `160`) |
| `format` | TEXT | NULL | Audio container format (`m4a`, `webm`) |
| `status` | TEXT | DEFAULT 'ready' | Ingestion status (`pending`, `ready`, `failed`) |
| `source` | TEXT | DEFAULT 'youtube' | Ingestion source provider |
| `created_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Record creation timestamp |
| `updated_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Last modification timestamp |

---

### 5. `lyrics` (Timed & Plain Lyrics)

Stores synchronized LRC timestamped lines and translated lyrics.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | TEXT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique lyric UUID |
| `track_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL, FK (tracks.id CASCADE) | Target track ID |
| `language` | TEXT | DEFAULT 'en' | ISO language code (`en`, `id`, `jp`) |
| `variant` | TEXT | DEFAULT 'original' | Variant type (`original`, `synced`, `translated`, `romanized`) |
| `content` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Raw LRC content with timestamp tags |
| `created_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Record creation timestamp |

---

### 6. `track_categories` (Track-Category Junction)

Many-to-many relationship mapping tracks to categories.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `track_id` | TEXT | PK, FK (tracks.id CASCADE) | Target track ID |
| `category_id` | TEXT | PK, FK (categories.id CASCADE) | Target category ID |

---

### 7. `track_artists` (Track-Artist Collaborations)

Many-to-many relationship mapping featured artists to tracks.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `track_id` | TEXT | PK, FK (tracks.id CASCADE) | Target track ID |
| `artist_id` | TEXT | PK, FK (artists.id CASCADE) | Featured artist ID |

---

### 8. `clients` (API Credentials)

Stores authorized client application keys and clearance levels.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | TEXT | PRIMARY KEY | Client UUID |
| `name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Client application name |
| `contact` | TEXT | NULL | Owner contact email or handle |
| `key_hash` | TEXT | UNIQUE, NOT NULL | SHA-256 hash of API key |
| `is_active` | INTEGER | DEFAULT 1 | Active flag (`1` enabled, `0` disabled) |
| `created_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Creation timestamp |
| `updated_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Last update timestamp |

---

### 9. `playlists` (User & Curated Playlists)

Stores playlist collections created by users or master admins.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | TEXT | PRIMARY KEY | Unique playlist UUID |
| `title` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Playlist title |
| `description` | TEXT | NULL | Playlist summary text |
| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Owner user ID |
| `cover_url` | TEXT | NULL | Playlist cover image URL |
| `created_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Creation timestamp |

---

### 10. `playlist_tracks` (Playlist Track Association)

Maps tracks inside playlists with sequence order.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `playlist_id` | TEXT | PK, FK (playlists.id CASCADE) | Playlist UUID |
| `track_id` | TEXT | PK, FK (tracks.id CASCADE) | Track UUID |
| `added_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Track addition timestamp |

---

### 11. `requests` (Song Ingestion Queue)

Stores track request queries submitted by listeners.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | TEXT | PRIMARY KEY | Request UUID |
| `query` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Search query (e.g. `Tulus - Monokrom`) |
| `status` | TEXT | DEFAULT 'pending' | Ingestion status (`pending`, `done`, `rejected`) |
| `metadata` | TEXT | NULL | Additional request JSON payload |
| `created_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Submission timestamp |

---

### 12. `maintenance` (Circuit Breaker State)

Stores system-wide maintenance mode switches.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `id` | TEXT | PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT 'global' | Global singleton ID |
| `lament` | INTEGER | DEFAULT 0 | Web frontend maintenance flag (`1` on, `0` off) |
| `lament_api` | INTEGER | DEFAULT 0 | Edge API maintenance flag (`1` on, `0` off) |
| `description` | TEXT | DEFAULT '' | Maintenance reason displayed to clients |
| `updated_at` | TEXT | NULL | Last modification timestamp |

---

---

### 13. `system_meta` (System State & Catalog Versioning)

Key-value store for global system metadata, including real-time catalog versioning for auto-sync.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `key` | TEXT | PRIMARY KEY | Configuration key (e.g. `catalog_version`) |
| `value` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Stored value (e.g. Unix timestamp) |
| `updated_at` | TEXT | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Last version update timestamp |

---

### 14. `lyrics_fts` (FTS5 Full-Text Search Virtual Table)

High-performance inverted index for instant sub-100ms lyrics search queries.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `track_id` | TEXT | UNINDEXED | Target track ID reference |
| `content` | TEXT | FTS5 Indexed | Tokenized lyrics body for `MATCH` lookups |

---

## Database Indexes

Lament utilizes 11 specialized B-Tree indexes for lightning-fast lookups and edge query performance:

- `idx_lyrics_track_id`: Index on `lyrics(track_id)` for high-speed lyric lookups.
- `idx_tracks_status_created`: Composite index on `tracks(status, created_at DESC)` for fast catalog pagination.
- `idx_tracks_title`: B-Tree index on `tracks(title)` for instant track title lookups.
- `idx_tracks_status_title`: Composite index on `tracks(status, title)` for active track search filtering.
- `idx_tracks_play_count`: Index on `tracks(play_count DESC)` for most-played and trending track queries.
- `idx_artists_name`: Index on `artists(name)` for artist name search queries.
- `idx_albums_title`: Index on `albums(title)` for album title search queries.
- `idx_track_artists_artist`: Index on `track_artists(artist_id)` for fast artist-to-track lookups.
- `idx_track_artists_track`: Index on `track_artists(track_id)` for fast track-to-artist resolution.
- `idx_track_categories_cat`: Index on `track_categories(category_id)` for category-based filtering.
- `idx_track_categories_track`: Index on `track_categories(track_id)` for track genre resolution.

---

## Automated Database Triggers

Lament leverages SQLite database-level triggers to guarantee real-time synchronization without manual scripts or external cron jobs:

### Lyrics FTS5 Synchronization
- `lyrics_ai`: `AFTER INSERT ON lyrics` &rarr; Automatically inserts new lyrics into `lyrics_fts`.
- `lyrics_au`: `AFTER UPDATE ON lyrics` &rarr; Updates matching entries in `lyrics_fts`.
- `lyrics_ad`: `AFTER DELETE ON lyrics` &rarr; Deletes matching entries from `lyrics_fts`.

### Catalog Version Auto-Bump (Auto-Sync)
- `tracks_catalog_ai`: `AFTER INSERT ON tracks` &rarr; Increments `catalog_version` in `system_meta`.
- `tracks_catalog_au`: `AFTER UPDATE ON tracks` &rarr; Increments `catalog_version` in `system_meta`.
- `tracks_catalog_ad`: `AFTER DELETE ON tracks` &rarr; Increments `catalog_version` in `system_meta`.

---

## Migrations & Local Schema Push

Push schema updates to Turso database:

```bash
cd lament-api
bun run db:push
```

